    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d640">

                <pb facs="0827" n="817" sameAs="frus:frus1947v07/pg817"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/4–547: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Smith</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-04-05T19:00:00+03:00">April 5, 1947—7
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 5—12:46 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1209. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kosmos</hi> 22. For Humelsine<anchor n="72"
                        xml:id="d640-f1"/> from Carter. Look at Department’s suggestion in third
                    paragraph of <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moskco</hi> 40<anchor n="73"
                        xml:id="d640-f2"/> re ammunition for China.</p>
                <p>Before the Secretary considers the matter further, he wishes to know character of
                    public announcement Department would make in case of sale of 7.92 mm
                    ammunition.</p>
                <p>Please wire me complete text of a proposed draft statement to support action
                    Department suggests.</p>
                <p>Understand clearly matter still completely exploratory. [Carter.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Smith</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d640-f1" n="72" xml:id="d640-f1-content">
                <p>Carlisle H. Humelsine, Director of the Office of Departmental Administration.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d640-f2" n="73" xml:id="d640-f2-content">
                <p>See telegram No. 773, April 2, 7 p.m., to the Ambassador in the Soviet Union,
                        <ref target="#pg814">p. 814</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
